{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"d451944b22f29442","name":"card_event_alpenfestung","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/WinterWar/events/card_event_alpenfestung","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"ALPENFESTUNG","text":"Set your HQ's defense to 25. Remove the top 10 cards of your deck.","flavorText":"The \"Alpenfestung\" was a German national redoubt planned by Reichsführer-SS Heinrich Himmler in November and December 1943. The plan was to establish a fortified \"Alpine Fortress\" in the mountainous regions of southern Germany and Austria as a final stand against the advancing Allied forces. However, it remained more of a symbolic idea born out of desperation rather than a practical or concrete plan. As the war progressed and the German military situation deteriorated, the actual implementation of the Alpine Fortress was not feasible due to resources shortages, the overwhelming Allied advance and the chaos within the German command structure. The alleged “Alpine Fortress” did affect the Allied planning during their advance towards Berlin, but when US forces entered Bavaria and western Austria in April 1945, not much organized resistance was met and it revealed the \"National Redoubt\" concept as a myth.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":7,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_alpenfestung","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_alpenfestung_title","SourceString":"ALPENFESTUNG","LocalizedString":"ALPENFESTUNG"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":7,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_alpenfestung_text","SourceString":"Set your HQ's defense to 25. Remove the top 10 cards of your deck.","LocalizedString":"Set your HQ's defense to 25. Remove the top 10 cards of your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_alpenfestung_history","SourceString":"The \"Alpenfestung\" was a German national redoubt planned by Reichsführer-SS Heinrich Himmler in November and December 1943. The plan was to establish a fortified \"Alpine Fortress\" in the mountainous regions of southern Germany and Austria as a final stand against the advancing Allied forces. However, it remained more of a symbolic idea born out of desperation rather than a practical or concrete plan. As the war progressed and the German military situation deteriorated, the actual implementation of the Alpine Fortress was not feasible due to resources shortages, the overwhelming Allied advance and the chaos within the German command structure. The alleged “Alpine Fortress” did affect the Allied planning during their advance towards Berlin, but when US forces entered Bavaria and western Austria in April 1945, not much organized resistance was met and it revealed the \"National Redoubt\" concept as a myth.","LocalizedString":"The \"Alpenfestung\" was a German national redoubt planned by Reichsführer-SS Heinrich Himmler in November and December 1943. The plan was to establish a fortified \"Alpine Fortress\" in the mountainous regions of southern Germany and Austria as a final stand against the advancing Allied forces. However, it remained more of a symbolic idea born out of desperation rather than a practical or concrete plan. As the war progressed and the German military situation deteriorated, the actual implementation of the Alpine Fortress was not feasible due to resources shortages, the overwhelming Allied advance and the chaos within the German command structure. The alleged “Alpine Fortress” did affect the Allied planning during their advance towards Berlin, but when US forces entered Bavaria and western Austria in April 1945, not much organized resistance was met and it revealed the \"National Redoubt\" concept as a myth."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Reinforcements'","ObjectPath"